Provenance notice

WELP (v1.0; carried unchanged into this v1.1.0 source release) is the
successor of the legacy WumboLabs WELP framework. The
successor implementation (welp_next/, tests/, docs/) was authored fresh under
the specification in SPEC.md. The following scientific assets are reused,
adapted, or distilled from the legacy framework under the selective reuse
decisions recorded in SPEC.md §8, with original source identity and SHA-256
provenance retained in the successor project's provenance records:

- fixtures/reliability/welp-reliability-sample-20-v3.json (REUSE)
- fixtures/quality/welp-quality-screen-12-v1.json (REUSE)
- fixtures/useful_context/multidocument.json, family-a.json (REUSE)
- fixtures/real_work/*.json task definitions (REUSE)
- fixtures/review/*.json review-qualification fixtures (REUSE)
- fixtures/agentic/{qualification,repository,system,research}/ task suites,
  workspaces, evaluators (REUSE)
- welp_next/agentic.py harness core (ADAPT of legacy harness/agentic.py:
  bubblewrap sandbox, adapters, tools, durable transcripts; outcome emission
  realigned to the successor methodology)
- welp_next/scorers/score_reliability.py (REUSE) and
  welp_next/scorers/safety_review.py (ADAPT of the legacy rubric-adjudication
  scorer: one qualified rubric evaluator by default plus at most one bounded
  escalation review)
- Contract semantics (outcomes, workload budgets, review rubric/boundary,
  reliability, context, agentic, real-work) are carried as normative semantic
  references distilled into SPEC.md; the legacy contract-version matrix is
  not carried forward.

Reused assets were extracted as verified copies, never imported in place at
run time. The successor carries no legacy execution-compatibility requirement
and does not validate legacy bundles.
